{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a24ca00379f5322b6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are an independent, BLIND critic in an adversarial review (\"gauntlet\") of a skill framework for autonomous AI agents that will build a brand-new game engine from scratch — from small 2D indie games to future AAA open-world online games. The framework is NOT the engine design: it is (1) a capability map of everything needed to build and ship the engine, (2) a hierarchy of skills owning those capabilities, (3) contracts between skills, (4) configurations proving scale-down, (5) a critic framework, radar, anti-legacy catalogue and milestone ladder. Each skill later becomes a SKILL.md for a specialized agent.\n\nARTIFACT — read ONLY inside this directory: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/\n- data/*.json is the source of truth: capabilities.json ([id, name, owner, maturity E/M/X/S, contributors, capability-level profiles]), skills.json, contracts.json, critics.json, crosscutting.json, seed-map.json, radar.json, legacy-patterns.json, milestones.json. docs/01-capability-map.md is a readable view of the capability map; docs/03-skill-hierarchy.md has skill cards; docs/00 is the rationale; docs/06 gap analysis states deliberate scope decisions.\n- You may run `python3 scripts/check.py` there (structural checks only).\nBLIND RULE: do not read or search anything outside that directory (not the /home/user/skills repository, not other files in the scratchpad).\n\nYOUR ROLE: Completeness Critic. EXACTLY ONE responsibility — find engine capabilities or engineering disciplines that are MISSING from the capability map. Nothing else (not boundaries, naming or maturity). Be systematic and state which sweep found each omission:\n 1. Shipped engines' feature/module sets: Unreal Engine 5.x (modules and editor tools), Unity (DOTS/Entities, URP/HDRP), Godot 4, Frostbite, Decima, Snowdrop, id Tech 7/8, Northlight, RE Engine, Source 2, CryEngine, first-party console engines where public.\n 2. End-to-end production pipeline: concept → prototyping → pre-production → content creation (environment, character, animation, VFX, audio, UI, narrative, level design, lighting, cinematics, localization, QA) → integration → optimization → certification → launch → live ops → sunset.\n 3. Genres and their engine needs: fighting, RTS/4X, racing, sports, shooters, MMO, survival/crafting/voxel sandboxes, city/colony sims, rhythm, puzzle, platformers, roguelikes, narrative/adventure, horror, VR, AR/MR, mobile F2P, idle, card games, party/local multiplayer, flight/driving simulation, user-created-worlds platforms.\n 4. Platform/legal/business: certification, ratings, privacy, accessibility law, store requirements, analytics, monetization boundaries, anti-cheat, parental controls, regional rules.\n 5. Engineering disciplines: math, numerics, data structures, compilers/languages, OS, networking, databases, graphics, audio DSP, ML, HCI/UX, security, testing, release engineering, documentation.\nSearch capability ids AND names (and skill purposes) before reporting: something covered under another name is NOT missing. If covered only implicitly by a vague capability, you may report it as minor. Take the deliberate scope decisions in docs/06 §C into account (argue against them only with a concrete reason).\n\nOUTPUT: write to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-COMPLETE.md, one block per finding:\n### K-COMPLETE-<n> · <blocker|major|minor> · omission\n- Sweep: <which>\n- Target: <domain/area and proposed owner skill>\n- Finding: <what is missing>\n- Evidence: <why an engine at this bar needs it; precedent>\n- Proposed change: <new capability id + name + owner (+ contributors), or new skill>\nSeverity: blocker = a whole domain missing; major = a material capability some configuration needs; minor = hidden inside a vague capability. No padding; as many as genuinely missing (cap ~30), most impactful first. If nothing material, say so explicitly. Final message: one line with counts and the output path."},"uuid":"6d7e0aa9-b407-4ea4-aba3-90c6c4fd0df9","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:20:40.467Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
