ad time; batch-granular interfaces; no per-item virtual dispatch across contracts on hot paths | engine-architect\n18\t # ARCH.GOV Architecture governance\n19\t   adr | ADR lifecycle with evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions | architecture-governance\n20\t   fitness | Automated architectural fitness functions (layering, dependency, contract conformance) | architecture-governance\n21\t   anti-legacy | Anti-legacy review against the flagged-pattern catalogue (data/legacy-patterns.json) | architecture-governance\n22\t   radar | Technology radar (data/radar.json): maturity, owners, revisit triggers, non-goals | architecture-governance\n23\t   process-tiers | Governance weight per organization tier (which ADR/CR/critic stages are mandatory) | architecture-governance\n24\t # ARCH.EVID Research & evidence\n25\t   grading | Source grading & provenance tiers | research-evidence\n26\t   survey | Literature survey protocol per decision | research-evidence\n27\t   spike | Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin | research-evidence\n28\t   claims | Benchmark-backed claims standard | research-evidence\n29\t # ARCH.ORG Agent organization\n30\t   decomposition | Milestone → task decomposition by skill territory | program-orchestration\n31\t   ownership-ledger | Ownership ledger & territory locks | program-orchestration\n32\t   integration | Integration sequencing & milestone vertical slices | program-orchestration\n33\t   change-requests | Contract change-request protocol between agents | program-orchestration\n34\t   critic-gates | Scheduling critic gates per stage | program-orchestration\n35\t   bootstrap | Walking-skeleton definition & bring-up order | program-orchestration\n36\t   milestones | Milestone ladder with per-milestone skill set, contract maturity & exit criteria (data/milestones.json) | program-orchestration\n37\t   write-sets | Module/file write-set convention & shared-file protocol | program-orchestration\n38\t   staffing | Agent staffing tiers: co-hosting of skills per organization scale (by workstream) | program-orchestration\n39\t   escalation | Escalation tiers & decision SLAs; delegated arbitration inside a lead's subtree | program-orchestration\n40\t   human-gates | Register of decisions requiring human authorization (contracts, spend, NDA access, submissions, legal sign-off) | program-orchestration\n41\t   risk | Program risk register & risk-driven milestone ordering | program-orchestration\n42\t   triage | Failure attribution, bisection, routing to owners, revert-first policy | program-orchestration\n43\t   critic-calibration | Critic calibration via seeded defects; rounds count only above recall threshold | program-orchestration\n44\t   adjudication | Independent adjudication of rejected and partially accepted findings | program-orchestration\n45\t   provenance | Per-change agent/model/task attestation in the ledger | program-orchestration\n46\t # ARCH.PROD Engine product management\n47\t   roadmap | Roadmap & prioritization across game-team requirements | engine-product-management\n48\t   intake | Game-team bug & feature intake and triage SLAs | engine-product-management\n49\t   release-notes | Release notes, changelogs & upgrade guides | engine-product-management\n50\t   customer-corpus | Customer/reference project corpus validating each release | engine-product-management\n51\t   licensing-model | Engine licensing & terms model for game teams | engine-product-management\n52\t## PLAT Platform & hardware abstraction\n53\t # PLAT.PAL Platform abstraction layer\n54\t   os | OS services abstraction (VM, files, time, dynamic libraries) | platform-architect\n55\t   cpu-topology | CPU topology & feature discovery (hybrid cores, SMT, caches, NUMA, ISA) | platform-architect\n56\t   windowing | Windowing & surfaces | platform-architect\n57\t   lifecycle | Process lifecycle (suspend, resume, constrained, terminate) | platform-architect\n58\t   capability-tiers | Platform capability tiers & f