olation | frame-orchestration\n216\t   time | Time domains (real, game, dilation, pause) & clocks | frame-orchestration\n217\t   latency | Input-to-photon latency & frame pacing (Reflex / Anti-Lag class) | frame-orchestration\n218\t   async-work | Multi-frame asynchronous work | frame-orchestration\n219\t   headless | Headless / server tick model | frame-orchestration\n220\t   access-model | Unified access declarations for all phase work (ECS and service resources) with derived ordering | frame-orchestration\n221\t   channels | Cross-subsystem data channels (C-FLOW) | frame-orchestration\n222\t   sim-schedule | Canonical simulation phase order (pre/post-physics, substeps, net snapshot, render extract) | frame-orchestration\n223\t   amortized | Time-sliced / rate-bucketed ticking & per-phase tick budgets | frame-orchestration\n224\t   critical-path | Frame critical-path analysis & phase-overlap reporting | frame-orchestration\n225\t   test-clock | Injectable/controllable clocks for tests | frame-orchestration\n226\t   phase-violations | Detection of writes to data owned by another phase | frame-orchestration\n227\t   present-timeline | Present timeline, pacing feedback & interposed presenters (C-PRESENT) | frame-orchestration\n228\t # CORE.OBJ Object model & identity\n229\t   identity | Entity identity (generational IDs, stable GUIDs) | entity-object-model\n230\t   hybrid | Hybrid object-model policy (ECS vs services vs asset objects vs UI objects) | entity-object-model\n231\t   references | Reference kinds & explicit lifetime (owner + generational handles; no tracing GC over engine objects; script references are weak handles) | entity-object-model\n232\t   events | Events & messaging: deferred, batched delivery at declared consumption points by default | entity-object-model\n233\t # CORE.ECS Entity component system\n234\t   storage | Component storage (archetype chunks vs sparse sets) | ecs-runtime\n235\t   queries | Queries & filters | ecs-runtime\n236\t   change |