ct | render-architect\n410\t   scene-sync | Simulation→render extraction: change-tracked, parallel, versioned delta streams (CPU cost O(changes)) | render-architect\n411\t   scalability | Render scalability tiers | render-architect\n412\t   multiview | Multi-view rendering: split-screen, PiP, captures, stereo/multiview and N-view (autostereo/light-field) outputs | render-architect\n413\t   debug-modes | Buffer visualization & render debug modes | render-architect\n414\t   submission-strategy | Submission strategy per hardware tier (GPU-driven vs CPU-culled batched), by ADR; TBDR suitability | render-architect\n415\t   editor-rendering | Editor render features: GPU picking, selection outline, editor primitives, preview scenes & thumbnails | render-architect\n416\t   instance-data | GPU instance data layout & delta upload | render-architect\n417\t # RND.RHI Hardware interface\n418\t   queues | Command recording & queues | rhi-core\n419\t   sync | GPU synchronization (timeline fences, enhanced barriers) | rhi-core\n420\t   pso | Pipeline-state models & caches (PSO, pipeline libraries, shader objects), async creation | rhi-core\n421\t   present | Swapchain, present modes, VRR | rhi-core\n422\t   caps | GPU capability tiers & feature detection | rhi-core\n423\t   crash | GPU fault instrumentation: breadcrumbs, markers, dump generation, device-lost recovery | rhi-core\n424\t   queries | Timestamp & pipeline-statistics queries | rhi-core\n425\t   workarounds | Vendor & driver workaround management | rhi-core\n426\t   binding-tiers | Binding-model tiers: bindless (default where capable) and bounded bind-group/descriptor-set tier | rhi-core\n427\t   implicit-sync | Implicit-synchronization backends (WebGPU): graph barrier output mapped or elided | rhi-core\n428\t   driver-policy | Driver version policy: minimum/known-bad drivers, deny-lists, user handling | rhi-core\n429\t   software-device | Null/software GPU device for headless CI (WARP/lavapipe/SwiftShader class) | rhi-co