urity\n1264\t   threats | Threat modeling | security-engineering\n1265\t   coding | Secure coding & memory-safety policy | security-engineering\n1266\t   trust | Trust boundaries for untrusted input | security-engineering\n1267\t   supply-chain | Supply-chain security (SBOM, signing, reproducible builds) | security-engineering\n1268\t   secrets | Secrets management | security-engineering\n1269\t   tamper | Anti-tamper & DRM boundary | security-engineering\n1270\t   privacy | Privacy engineering | security-engineering\n1271\t   sandbox | Mod / UGC sandbox policy | security-engineering\n1272\t   server-validation | Server-side cheat validation | anti-cheat-integrity\n1273\t   anticheat | Client anti-cheat middleware integration boundary | anti-cheat-integrity\n1274\t   abuse | Exploit & economy-abuse detection signals | anti-cheat-integrity\n1275\t   score-integrity | Leaderboard & achievement submission validation | anti-cheat-integrity\n1276\t   memory-safety | Memory-safety posture: hardened library modes, shipping bounds checks, memory-safe language for untrusted-input parsers, MTE/PAC | security-engineering\n1277\t   hardening | Exploit-mitigation & hardened-build matrix per platform (CFI, shadow stacks, allocator hardening) | security-engineering\n1278\t   crypto-policy | Cryptography & TLS/certificate policy | security-engineering\n1279\t   vuln-response | Vulnerability intake, disclosure, severity SLAs & patch path to shipped titles | security-engineering\n1280\t   incident | Live incident-response runbooks for online titles | security-engineering\n1281\t   dev-trust | Project/workspace trust, plugin signing & permissions, sandboxed import of untrusted source assets | security-engineering\n1282\t   agent-boundary | Development-agent capability scoping, sandboxing, egress & prompt-injection threat model | security-engineering\n1283\t   genai | Generative-feature threat model: prompt injection, output handling, PII, cost DoS | security-engineering\n1284\t   data